<title>FRANCE: NAmerican machinery top Paris air import in '96.</title>
<headline>NAmerican machinery top Paris air import in '96.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipments of machinery, motors, equipment and parts from North America was the leading import category and origin to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly in 1996, French Ministry of Transport (MoT) figures showed.</p>
<p>Other top ten imports by category and origin in tonnes were:</p>
<p>1996 traffic</p>
<p>    Region	Product	 Tonnage   Pct change on 95</p>
<p> 1. N.America   Machinery/     19,901    up   10.3</p>
<p>		    equipment/</p>
<p>		    parts</p>
<p> 2. Mid-East/   Machinery/     15,649    down 16.5</p>
<p>	Asia	equipment/</p>
<p>		    parts</p>
<p> 3. Africa	Vegetables     12,247    up    7.4</p>
<p> 4. Mid-East/   Travel goods/  12,192    down  3.6</p>
<p>	Asia	garments/hosiery</p>
<p>		    footwear</p>
<p> 5. N.America   Meat	     11,414    up    7.2</p>
<p> 6. Africa	Fruit &amp; Nuts    8,560    down  8.6</p>
<p> 7. Mid-East/   Assorted	  8,096    down  4.0</p>
<p>	 Africa   manufactured</p>
<p>		    goods</p>
<p> 8. N. America  Assorted	  7,363    up   10.6</p>
<p>		    manufactured</p>
<p>		    goods</p>
<p> 9. N. America  Fish &amp; Seafood  6,587    up    7.8</p>
<p>10. Central/    Meat		4,558    up   22.1</p>
<p>South America/</p>
<p>Caribbean</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
